1
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:34,560
(Recap)
Feels like we're escaping the apocalypse.

2
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:35,840
Like we're eloping.

3
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:36,600
They are

4
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,360
so sweet.

5
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,560
What do you wanna do right now?

6
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:39,240
Zone out.

7
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:40,080
Then let's zone out.

8
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,920
Two little space cadets.

9
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:43,960
I want to spend my time with them.

10
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,240
No closing your eyes.

11
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:46,880
Can't close my eyes?

12
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:48,780
(Holds hand)

13
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,080
I'm not great at expressing myself.

14
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,160
(Fang's Observation Notes)
So I wrote this.

15
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:57,440
They're a little too close.

16
00:00:58,680 --> 00:00:59,720
Thank you.

17
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,280
You have made me realize that,

18
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:02,400
besides Si,

19
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,560
(Xing)
I have you here in this city, too.

20
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,160
That line...

21
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,520
What?

22
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:10,680
You do it.

23
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,320
Let's do it together.

24
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:14,640
Want to go out tomorrow
or the day after?

25
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,080
Up to you.

26
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:16,960
Okay.

27
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:17,960
I'll go drop in
a Master Kong Jasmine coin.

28
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:21,960
He spent two coins

29
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,560
on her.

30
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,800
Isn't that love?

31
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,720
It is!

32
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,760
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

33
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,160
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

34
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,440
♪Set reality aside♪

35
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:32,760
♪Follow your heart♪

36
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,120
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

37
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,600
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

38
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,480
♪Just be a little braver♪

39
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:41,240
♪Come closer, come closer♪

40
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:44,320
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

41
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,440
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

42
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,160
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

43
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:54,340
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

44
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,460
(Badminton practice)

45
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:59,020
(A badminton court in Beijing)

46
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:10,440
So handsome.

47
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,760
This is like his home court.

48
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:13,800
He's in his element now.

49
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,840
Right in his comfort zone.

50
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:19,400
Chen Hewen looks so good.

51
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,060
Sha Yue'er is here.

52
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:22,640
(Sha Yue'er arrives)

53
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,320
He's shy.

54
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,080
Hello.

55
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,280
Hello.

56
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,520
You're playing alone?

57
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,080
Yeah, by myself.

58
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:33,400
Yeah.

59
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:35,580
(Laughs)

60
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:38,300
(Glances)

61
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,520
Why are you wearing such...

62
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,160
Such a soft pink today.

63
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:42,360
Yeah, why so pink?

64
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,600
You're so blue.

65
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,280
The flowers are for you.

66
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,560
Thank you.

67
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,880
New flowers.

68
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:48,520
Yeah.

69
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,400
Let me see.

70
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,520
Pretty.

71
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,240
Blue.

72
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:53,760
White and blue.

73
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,080
How are you so good at picking flowers?

74
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:56,400
Am I?

75
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:56,960
You are.

76
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,320
Every flower you've given me
is so pretty.

77
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,000
Right?

78
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,400
You're pretty good.

79
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,080
I'll put them here for now.

80
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,000
I don't think they'll stand up.

81
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:03,280
They won't.

82
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,120
That's why I put them here.

83
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:04,920
Okay.

84
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,840
Try this.
I just rewrapped your racket grip.

85
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,480
Thank you.

86
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,580
Did you eat anything today?

87
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:11,180
(Concerned)

88
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,840
I ate a lot at lunch.

89
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:14,040
Let's play for a bit.

90
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:14,520
Give it a try.

91
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,320
Let's play.

92
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:18,500
(Laughs)

93
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:19,520
Why is Chen Hewen

94
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:20,120
so shy?

95
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,360
You serve.

96
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,120
Same move as always.

97
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,960
It's okay. Take it slow.

98
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:31,800
I'll try to hit it right to you.

99
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,080
Okay.

100
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,800
Just feed it to the same spot.

101
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:42,840
You're pretty good.

102
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:44,920
Thanks.

103
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:45,840
(Happy)

104
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,560
Take this one.

105
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,680
Not bad. You're actually pretty good.

106
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:55,720
So you don't usually play badminton?

107
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,880
I really don't.

108
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,560
I only play with my dad once in a while.

109
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:01,960
So you've only played with your dad?

110
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:02,400
Just once in a while.

111
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,200
Like once a year.

112
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:07,360
Actually, I think you're pretty good.

113
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,880
Thanks.

114
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,560
I think I'm not bad either.

115
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,880
Sorry.

116
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,600
An arrow from Cupid.

117
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,120
It hit her.

118
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,600
Are you okay?

119
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,600
I'm probably gonna have a bump later.

120
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,520
Are you okay?

121
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,040
That really hurts.

122
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:32,720
I'm gonna pass out.

123
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,480
How did that happen?

124
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,760
Stay still.

125
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,940
I'm still.

126
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:42,540
(Standing still)

127
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,760
You gotta get the ball.

128
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:45,740
(Scratches head)

129
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,700
(Holding back laughter)
I seriously can't believe you.

130
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,880
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

131
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,720
You hit it right at me on purpose.

132
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,760
I didn't.

133
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,820
(Out-of-bounds ball)

134
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,120
What's that supposed to mean?

135
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,360
I did it on purpose.

136
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,480
You know
how to move your opponent around.

137
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,080
You even know to hit it to the left.

138
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,240
She's really good
at moving people around.

139
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:20,000
Pretty good, huh?

140
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,160
You even know how to do that.

141
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,560
Of course.

142
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,800
You got it.

143
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,840
Seriously, you're good.

144
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,120
You made me run all over the court.

145
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,320
You're even better.

146
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,960
It kind of feels like
watching them date.

147
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:46,640
It's that back-and-forth chemistry.

148
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:49,160
Are you tired?

149
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,120
A little.

150
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,880
Do you want some water or something?

151
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,240
Yeah.

152
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,160
Have some water.

153
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,120
Here, have this one.

154
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:57,880
(Helps open it)\Thank you.

155
00:05:59,240 --> 00:05:59,680
What's this?

156
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,160
This isn't mine.

157
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:00,600
This is...

158
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,400
Your memory really isn't that great.

159
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,960
See? You noticed. My memory...

160
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:07,500
(Glances)

161
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:11,560
Do you know what my name is?

162
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,660
(Asks)

163
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,120
"Sha Qi'er".

164
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,200
(Teasing)
"Sha Qi'er".

165
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,520
Why not just call her "Sha Qima"?

166
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,600
"Sha Qi'er"?

167
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,520
"Sha Qi'er".

168
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,960
That's so disrespectful.

169
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:27,680
We're out on a date,

170
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,480
and I don't even know

171
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,000
my date's name.

172
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,680
I'm the one who asked her out.

173
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,240
Why did I even ask her out?

174
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,600
Come on. Let's change and get some food.

175
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:34,880
Okay, let's go.

176
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:35,320
Sure.

177
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,160
What's this?

178
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,700
(Imitates)

179
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,200
You know how to do that too?

180
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:42,920
Of course.

181
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,640
This place.

182
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,200
Time to eat.

183
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,760
These are your favorites.

184
00:06:58,760 --> 00:06:59,840
I'm so hungry. They look so good.

185
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:00,720
They're pretty good.

186
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,600
They're making me hungry.

187
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:02,640
Have a seat. Sit.

188
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:03,240
Sit.

189
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:03,960
Here.

190
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:06,220
(Pulls the chair out)

191
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,240
Thanks.

192
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,680
Sha Yue'er looks so pretty in white.

193
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,280
The "first love" vibe.

194
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,560
Let's drink this.

195
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,680
Which one do you want?

196
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:22,840
You definitely want this one, right?

197
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:23,440
Yeah.

198
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:24,520
Thanks.

199
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,400
I'll open it for you.

200
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,260
(Helps open it)

201
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:28,600
Oh my gosh.

202
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,880
You even opened it for me.

203
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,680
Chen Hewen noticed

204
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,600
she really loves that one.

205
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,640
Oh, wait.

206
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:36,640
What's wrong?

207
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,000
This one.

208
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:40,720
It's for you.

209
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:41,240
Thanks.

210
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:41,840
A gift for you.

211
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:43,640
Because

212
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:45,320
I remember

213
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,200
you said you liked

214
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,200
Counterclockwise,

215
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,560
so I bought you

216
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,240
the vinyl.

217
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:50,360
Sha Yue'er,

218
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,120
do you have a favorite song

219
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:51,760
by Jay Chou?

220
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,280
Counterclockwise.

221
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,560
Counterclockwise?

222
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:01,660
(Look closely)

223
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,760
Yeah, this was his first album,

224
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,720
and the last song he recorded
for the album.

225
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,120
The one with Counterclockwise

226
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,280
on it.

227
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,280
Chen Hewen is so thoughtful.

228
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,360
Okay.

229
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,160
Thank you.

230
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:20,240
Why don't we put it in that bag for now?

231
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,200
Put it over there with you.

232
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,680
Okay, thanks.

233
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,140
(Carefully puts it away)

234
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,160
Why don't you eat a little first?

235
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,680
Just have something to tide you over.

236
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:33,600
Let's dig in.

237
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,560
- Let's just dig in.
- What's this?

238
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,080
It's egg.

239
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,720
Let me cut it for you.

240
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:42,720
So thoughtful.

241
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,920
You really know
how to take care of people.

242
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:46,800
Yeah, help yourself.

243
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,000
Okay.

244
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,960
Thanks.

245
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:51,840
It's pretty good.

246
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:54,080
It's really good.

247
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:55,100
(Thumbs up)

248
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:59,080
So, how did you think

249
00:08:59,080 --> 00:08:59,520
you played today?

250
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:00,360
Pretty good.

251
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,480
That was my first time ever going
to a badminton court.

252
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,240
First time?

253
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,520
Yeah.

254
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,640
It was pretty fun.

255
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,320
But I think you played really well.

256
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,760
I think so too.

257
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:12,320
For someone

258
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,440
who was at a badminton court
for the first time.

259
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,240
Yeah, you did really well.

260
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,800
What else do you do in your daily life?

261
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,560
Besides work, I exercise.

262
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,880
I play badminton more
than anything else.

263
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:24,680
Badminton is probably both my job

264
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,960
and something I really love.

265
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,240
I just wanted you to get a sense of

266
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,640
what my everyday life is like.

267
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,120
I spend a lot of my time

268
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,200
playing badminton.

269
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,000
So it means something

270
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,840
a little different to me.

271
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,240
My mom used to train at a sports school.

272
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:43,280
She specialized in badminton.

273
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,000
My mom was actually

274
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:46,840
really good back then.

275
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,800
I just happened to try it once,

276
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,960
and I thought it was pretty fun.

277
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,600
I'm relatively tall,

278
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,040
and then...

279
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,080
Yeah.

280
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:58,640
Don't laugh.

281
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:00,600
Okay.

282
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,520
I feel like I can control

283
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:03,440
how fast the shuttle goes.

284
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,160
I really like that feeling

285
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,400
of being in control.

286
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:06,520
(Glances)

287
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,000
They both are.

288
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,080
We were supposed to play

289
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,120
at my own badminton court today.

290
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,120
But my court

291
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,480
isn't ready yet.

292
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,640
It's okay.

293
