00:50:34,240 --> 00:50:35,960
It looks delicious.

1434
00:50:41,560 --> 00:50:42,520
Sweet and tangy.

1435
00:50:47,480 --> 00:50:48,560
It's not crispy anymore.

1436
00:50:50,940 --> 00:50:51,820
(Observes)

1437
00:50:51,840 --> 00:50:53,680
I think I used too little starch too.

1438
00:50:57,000 --> 00:50:58,360
Was this your first time making it?

1439
00:50:59,040 --> 00:51:00,520
Then you did really well.

1440
00:51:00,520 --> 00:51:01,300
(Good review)

1441
00:51:15,960 --> 00:51:17,720
Doesn't this dish take at least

1442
00:51:17,720 --> 00:51:18,800
an hour?

1443
00:51:19,240 --> 00:51:21,560
Just soaking the starch takes forever.

1444
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:23,200
That's what you soaked this morning?

1445
00:51:23,560 --> 00:51:25,160
Yeah, then you marinate the meat.

1446
00:51:25,160 --> 00:51:25,840
Let me think.

1447
00:51:25,840 --> 00:51:28,000
I think it's three spoonfuls of sugar...

1448
00:51:28,000 --> 00:51:28,760
(Recites the recipe)

1449
00:51:28,760 --> 00:51:30,120
Three spoonfuls of water,

1450
00:51:30,120 --> 00:51:31,160
four spoonfuls of rice vinegar,

1451
00:51:31,160 --> 00:51:32,760
a little light soy sauce and salt,

1452
00:51:32,760 --> 00:51:34,540
(Nods)
two spoonfuls of cornstarch.

1453
00:51:34,560 --> 00:51:35,040
Then fry it.

1454
00:51:35,040 --> 00:51:36,520
After frying,

1455
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:38,480
cook the sauce in some oil,

1456
00:51:38,480 --> 00:51:39,640
then add the meat.

1457
00:51:39,640 --> 00:51:42,160
Then add the veggies.

1458
00:51:42,160 --> 00:51:43,200
He memorized the whole thing.

1459
00:51:43,200 --> 00:51:44,160
(Laughs)
Then it's all grown up.

1460
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:44,640
Yeah.

1461
00:51:44,640 --> 00:51:45,760
A fully grown dish.

1462
00:51:45,760 --> 00:51:46,960
Yeah, all grown up.

1463
00:51:47,100 --> 00:51:48,500
(Pinches)

1464
00:51:49,720 --> 00:51:51,840
It tastes just as good as store-bought.

1465
00:51:52,260 --> 00:51:53,380
(Compliments)

1466
00:51:54,000 --> 00:51:55,040
Not quite.

1467
00:51:55,040 --> 00:51:55,760
He's shy now.

1468
00:51:58,680 --> 00:52:00,040
So we have to finish everything.

1469
00:52:00,040 --> 00:52:01,480
Finish what's in your bowl.

1470
00:52:02,240 --> 00:52:04,200
Okay, I will.

1471
00:52:10,960 --> 00:52:12,160
Did you go to the hospital again?

1472
00:52:12,780 --> 00:52:13,480
(Hands over a tissue)

1473
00:52:13,480 --> 00:52:14,560
How's Xing today?

1474
00:52:14,880 --> 00:52:16,400
She's doing better.

1475
00:52:16,680 --> 00:52:18,520
I'd say another week

1476
00:52:18,520 --> 00:52:19,360
at most.

1477
00:52:19,520 --> 00:52:20,040
Right?

1478
00:52:21,240 --> 00:52:23,520
I'm basically their carrier pigeon now.

1479
00:52:23,680 --> 00:52:24,820
(Carrier pigeon)
I'm the messenger.

1480
00:52:26,880 --> 00:52:27,760
Xing also told us

1481
00:52:27,760 --> 00:52:28,960
to make sure we eat more.

1482
00:52:29,560 --> 00:52:30,560
Eat more.

1483
00:52:30,560 --> 00:52:32,040
Then I'll have more.

1484
00:52:33,560 --> 00:52:34,160
Here, have this.

1485
00:52:34,160 --> 00:52:34,760
Okay.

1486
00:52:34,760 --> 00:52:36,020
(Serves food)

1487
00:52:37,140 --> 00:52:38,700
(Serves food)
Feeding each other.

1488
00:52:39,120 --> 00:52:40,200
Eat the meat.

1489
00:52:40,200 --> 00:52:41,060
(Serves food x2)

1490
00:52:41,960 --> 00:52:42,960
Okay.

1491
00:52:43,400 --> 00:52:44,340
You eat too.

1492
00:52:44,340 --> 00:52:45,280
(Serves food x2)
Here.

1493
00:52:45,840 --> 00:52:46,240
Okay.

1494
00:52:49,200 --> 00:52:50,000
Grilled mushrooms.

1495
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:50,540
(Serves food x3)

1496
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:53,200
You need to eat more.

1497
00:52:53,800 --> 00:52:55,240
You need to eat more.

1498
00:52:55,940 --> 00:52:56,940
(Serves food x4)

1499
00:52:56,980 --> 00:52:57,640
(Serves food x3)

1500
00:52:57,640 --> 00:52:58,240
Thanks.

1501
00:52:59,140 --> 00:52:59,740
(Serves food x5)

1502
00:53:00,760 --> 00:53:01,640
This is hilarious.

1503
00:53:03,000 --> 00:53:03,800
What else?

1504
00:53:05,280 --> 00:53:08,220
(Cui Yihang's bowl)
They're both like, stop giving me food.

1505
00:53:08,260 --> 00:53:10,020
(Wu Siying's bowl)

1506
00:53:10,200 --> 00:53:11,000
I don't want any more.

1507
00:53:12,640 --> 00:53:14,000
Then have this mushroom.

1508
00:53:14,480 --> 00:53:15,600
This one's for you.

1509
00:53:15,840 --> 00:53:16,840
You don't like it?

1510
00:53:18,200 --> 00:53:19,000
I do.

1511
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:19,440
But I...

1512
00:53:19,440 --> 00:53:20,400
Just eat it.

1513
00:53:21,120 --> 00:53:22,240
It suits you better.

1514
00:53:22,240 --> 00:53:23,560
Why are they fighting over who eats it?

1515
00:53:23,560 --> 00:53:24,800
You eat it.

1516
00:53:26,480 --> 00:53:28,680
Earlier, we cooked some
of Xing's dumplings.

1517
00:53:30,240 --> 00:53:31,480
They were pretty good.

1518
00:53:32,360 --> 00:53:33,080
For New Year's,

1519
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:34,640
do you put anything
inside your dumplings?

1520
00:53:35,160 --> 00:53:36,680
We put almonds in them.

1521
00:53:37,480 --> 00:53:39,160
I thought you meant coins.

1522
00:53:39,160 --> 00:53:39,480
No.

1523
00:53:39,480 --> 00:53:41,160
If you get one, you're the lucky one.

1524
00:53:41,260 --> 00:53:42,700
(Little almond, lucky one)

1525
00:53:44,760 --> 00:53:47,040
Lucky one.

1526
00:53:48,480 --> 00:53:49,760
If you get one, you're the lucky one.

1527
00:53:49,760 --> 00:53:52,620
(Little almond, lucky one)

1528
00:53:54,080 --> 00:53:54,720
Like that?

1529
00:53:54,720 --> 00:53:55,240
Yeah.

1530
00:53:55,600 --> 00:53:57,280
Who got one last year?

1531
00:53:57,560 --> 00:53:59,680
We put in a lot.

1532
00:53:59,680 --> 00:54:00,760
So you're all lucky ones.

1533
00:54:01,840 --> 00:54:02,920
A whole family of lucky ones.

1534
00:54:03,440 --> 00:54:04,000
Yeah.

1535
00:54:04,000 --> 00:54:05,000
A whole family of lucky ones.

1536
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:06,240
(A whole family of lucky ones)

1537
00:54:06,240 --> 00:54:07,280
Let's try it this year.

1538
00:54:07,280 --> 00:54:07,860
(Let's try it this year)

1539
00:54:12,400 --> 00:54:13,240
These two...

1540
00:54:14,360 --> 00:54:15,400
Let's try it this year.

1541
00:54:15,400 --> 00:54:18,340
(A whole family of lucky ones,
let's try it this year)

1542
00:54:24,080 --> 00:54:25,040
I'm really full.

1543
00:54:25,040 --> 00:54:26,840
Let's go check over there.

1544
00:54:26,840 --> 00:54:27,600
Okay.

1545
00:54:28,880 --> 00:54:30,160
Look at this little cat.

1546
00:54:30,960 --> 00:54:33,080
(Cake brought by Wu Siying)
Should we take a picture with it?

1547
00:54:35,980 --> 00:54:37,580
(Leans close)

1548
00:54:39,100 --> 00:54:39,820
(Pouts)

1549
00:54:39,840 --> 00:54:40,760
So cute.

1550
00:54:41,240 --> 00:54:42,080
Looks good.

1551
00:54:42,080 --> 00:54:42,680
So good.

1552
00:54:42,680 --> 00:54:44,680
Honestly, none of these
really look like me.

1553
00:54:45,060 --> 00:54:46,120
(Covers mouth and laughs)
Actually, yeah.

1554
00:54:46,120 --> 00:54:46,800
Right.

1555
00:54:46,940 --> 00:54:48,160
(Covers mouth and laughs)

1556
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:50,280
We're starting
to talk more and more alike.

1557
00:54:57,600 --> 00:54:58,560
There are stars.

1558
00:54:59,240 --> 00:54:59,880
Look closely.

1559
00:54:59,880 --> 00:55:01,160
There are so many over here.

1560
00:55:01,160 --> 00:55:03,080
(Leans together)
Even the balcony feels crowded now.

1561
00:55:10,840 --> 00:55:11,640
Did you see

1562
00:55:11,640 --> 00:55:12,640
the message I sent you yesterday?

1563
00:55:14,120 --> 00:55:14,760
I did.

1564
00:55:16,280 --> 00:55:16,920
It was really touching.

1565
00:55:17,600 --> 00:55:18,240
Really touching.

1566
00:55:20,840 --> 00:55:21,520
Really?

1567
00:55:22,800 --> 00:55:24,760
Seriously. It made me cry.

1568
00:55:24,780 --> 00:55:25,540
(Joking)

1569
00:55:26,080 --> 00:55:28,040
That sounds totally made up.

1570
00:55:32,080 --> 00:55:32,800
It's not.

1571
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:36,000
They're so cute.

1572
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:37,080
So cute.

1573
00:55:37,640 --> 00:55:39,440
Want me to cover you
with the blanket a little?

1574
00:55:39,440 --> 00:55:40,520
Are you cold?

1575
00:55:47,880 --> 00:55:48,520
When there's a problem,

1576
00:55:48,520 --> 00:55:49,920
do you just say it?

1577
00:55:51,240 --> 00:55:51,800
Yeah.

1578
00:55:53,400 --> 00:55:54,240
Sometimes if you don't,

1579
00:55:54,240 --> 00:55:55,520
the misunderstanding just gets worse.

1580
00:55:56,000 --> 00:55:56,840
If you say it outright,

1581
00:55:56,840 --> 00:55:58,720
you might solve it right away.

1582
00:55:59,360 --> 00:56:00,280
Well said.

1583
00:56:00,280 --> 00:56:00,680
Yeah.

1584
00:56:01,600 --> 00:56:03,600
So are you usually

1585
00:56:03,600 --> 00:56:04,840
pretty expressive,

1586
00:56:04,840 --> 00:56:06,400
or more reserved?

1587
00:56:07,080 --> 00:56:08,560
Emotionally.

1588
00:56:09,280 --> 00:56:10,280
How do I put it?

1589
00:56:11,440 --> 00:56:13,840
I'm not exactly reserved.

1590
00:56:14,640 --> 00:56:15,480
If I can feel

1591
00:56:15,480 --> 00:56:17,040
what the other person feels,

1592
00:56:18,480 --> 00:56:20,880
that they like and care about me,

1593
00:56:22,640 --> 00:56:25,840
I'll show it back even more.

1594
00:56:27,000 --> 00:56:29,960
I'll let them know in my own way.

1595
00:56:33,040 --> 00:56:34,200
I think maybe

1596
00:56:34,200 --> 00:56:35,480
I go more by feeling.

1597
00:56:36,760 --> 00:56:37,640
Then how do you know

1598
00:56:37,640 --> 00:56:38,800
if that feeling's right?

1599
00:56:41,520 --> 00:56:42,960
First, you ask yourself

1600
00:56:42,960 --> 00:56:44,840
when you're together,

1601
00:56:45,360 --> 00:56:47,360
are you always giving in?

1602
00:56:47,360 --> 00:56:50,640
Or are you always

1603
00:56:50,640 --> 00:56:51,960
the more accommodating one?

1604
00:56:53,560 --> 00:56:54,560
It's okay for a while,

1605
00:56:54,560 --> 00:56:56,080
but not long-term.

1606
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:56,840
Exactly.

1607
00:56:57,160 --> 00:56:57,880
Yeah.

1608
00:56:59,160 --> 00:57:01,320
But our time
in the house is pretty short.

1609
00:57:02,560 --> 00:57:04,640
You've thought this through pretty well.

1610
00:57:08,560 --> 00:57:10,040
Do you feel like, with us,

1611
00:57:10,040 --> 00:57:11,600
you've had to give in?

1612
00:57:13,640 --> 00:57:14,720
Not really.

1613
00:57:14,720 --> 00:57:16,700
(Doesn't feel like he's been giving in)

1614
00:57:17,720 --> 00:57:20,000
So I haven't felt

1615
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:22,160
like I've had to give in either.

1616
00:57:22,160 --> 00:57:23,640
(I haven't felt that either)
I think it's been really nice.

1617
00:57:23,640 --> 00:57:25,660
(I think it's been really nice)

1618
00:57:28,560 --> 00:57:29,640
What?

1619
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:31,080
Did you not hear me,

1620
00:57:31,080 --> 00:57:32,680
or do you want me to say it again?

1621
00:57:34,280 --> 00:57:35,280
I wanna hear it again.

1622
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:43,800
No.

1623
00:57:53,880 --> 00:57:55,320
How do you know

1624
00:57:57,120 --> 00:57:58,640
if you like someone?

1625
00:58:03,200 --> 00:58:04,560
I think it's whether you instinctively

1626
00:58:04,560 --> 00:58:06,040
want to be close to them.

1627
00:58:15,440 --> 00:58:16,960
Instinctively wanting to be close.

1628
00:58:18,840 --> 00:58:19,720
What about you?

1629
00:58:21,120 --> 00:58:23,120
Definitely wanting to be close to them.

1630
00:58:24,120 --> 00:58:26,960
And when I'm not thinking
about anything,

1631
00:58:26,960 --> 00:58:28,520
I'll suddenly picture

1632
00:58:28,520 --> 00:58:32,160
their face and the way they look.

1633
00:58:36,720 --> 00:58:37,880
I'm thinking about

1634
00:58:37,880 --> 00:58:39,000
whether I look forward

1635
00:58:39,000 --> 00:58:40,200
to coming home more every day.

1636
00:58:44,800 --> 00:58:46,720
And thinking about it, I think I do.

1637
00:58:54,440 --> 00:58:56,000
I look forward to getting
to know you better.

1638
00:58:56,000 --> 00:58:59,340
(Every day, I look forward to coming
home and getting to know you more)

1639
00:59:00,360 --> 00:59:01,240
Funny enough,

1640
00:59:02,680 --> 00:59:03,320
it's like

1641
00:59:03,320 --> 00:59:05,360
whenever I get back early,

1642
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:07,520
everyone comes back one by one,

1643
00:59:08,080 --> 00:59:09,520
but it's different when you come back.

1644
00:59:14,640 --> 00:59:16,440
These past two days,
I've been so happy to see you.

1645
00:59:17,520 --> 00:59:18,400
Me too.

1646
00:59:31,160 --> 00:59:31,680
So sweet.

1647
00:59:31,840 --> 00:59:32,840
Pure happiness.

1648
00:59:33,000 --> 00:59:33,480
Lucky one.

1649
00:59:33,680 --> 00:59:35,360
(Little almonds, lucky ones)
We're all lucky ones.

1650
00:59:35,520 --> 00:59:36,760
Lucky ones.

1651
00:59:37,080 --> 00:59:38,320
So thoughtful.

1652
00:59:38,480 --> 00:59:39,560
I feel like these two

1653
00:59:39,560 --> 00:59:40,840
have a different vibe

1654
00:59:40,840 --> 00:59:41,940
from everyone else.

1655
00:59:41,940 --> 00:59:42,800
(What do you mean?)

1656
00:59:42,800 --> 00:59:43,160
They're

1657
00:59:43,160 --> 00:59:44,520
subtly sweet.

1658
00:59:45,320 --> 00:59:46,200
That's the vibe.

1659
00:59:46,200 --> 00:59:47,040
Are they sweet?

1660
00:59:47,040 --> 00:59:47,920
Yeah.

1661
00:59:47,920 --> 00:59:49,380
But subtly sweet.

1662
00:59:49,380 --> 00:59:50,500
(A sweetness you have to savor)
When Cui Yihang and Si

1663
00:59:50,500 --> 00:59:51,120
are together,

1664
00:59:51,120 --> 00:59:52,600
even their voices get softer.

1665
00:59:52,600 --> 00:59:53,800
It's so peaceful.

1666
00:59:53,800 --> 00:59:54,120
Yeah.

1667
00:59:54,120 --> 00:59:54,560
He

1668
00:59:54,560 --> 00:59:56,440
turns into such a sweet boy.

1669
00:59:57,240 --> 00:59:58,200
It feels like Si and Xing

1670
00:59:58,200 --> 00:59:59,600
have a purifying power.

1671
00:59:59,600 --> 01:00:02,120
(Si and Xing have purifying superpowers)
Anyone who gets close to them

1672
01:00:02,120 --> 01:00:03,120
just softens up.

1673
01:00:03,120 --> 01:00:05,520
You don't see
this kind of romance often.

1674
01:00:05,520 --> 01:00:06,880
It's really shy and sweet.

1675
01:00:13,360 --> 01:00:16,480
♪Please come back♪

1676
01:00:16,480 --> 01:00:21,310
(Today's letter from Wu Xingying)
♪I can't bear this alone♪

1677
01:00:21,320 --> 01:00:22,960
Let's see what Xing wrote.

1678
01:00:27,360 --> 01:00:29,080
What's up? Why are you so happy?

1679
01:00:29,520 --> 01:00:30,280
I'm reading her letter.

1680
01:00:34,320 --> 01:00:35,480
Sun Bohan.

1681
01:00:35,920 --> 01:00:37,720
Such a wholesome smile.

1682
01:00:40,440 --> 01:00:42,120
Look at you bouncing your leg.

1683
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:44,120
He's pretty happy.

1684
01:00:44,440 --> 01:00:46,520
One little leg bounce
and he's all energized.

1685
01:00:46,520 --> 01:00:47,920
Sun Bohan,

1686
01:00:47,920 --> 01:00:49,640
I got the plant you sent

1687
01:00:49,640 --> 01:00:50,840
and really love it.

1688
01:00:50,840 --> 01:00:53,160
Everyone stops to look at it.

1689
01:00:53,160 --> 01:00:54,480
Even the doctors and nurses

1690
01:00:54,480 --> 01:00:55,960
stop and look for a while.

1691
01:00:57,000 --> 01:00:57,520
That made him happy.

1692
01:00:57,960 --> 01:00:59,400
Remember when we went boating?

1693
01:00:59,400 --> 01:01:00,640
There were little specks of light
on the river.

1694
01:01:01,120 --> 01:01:02,560
This has them too.

1695
01:01:02,560 --> 01:01:03,760
I'll take good care of it.

1696
01:01:05,380 --> 01:01:06,580
(The night before)

1697
01:01:06,600 --> 01:01:08,920
This is my second letter to Xing.

1698
01:01:09,240 --> 01:01:10,160
So much to say, so little paper.

1699
01:01:10,160 --> 01:01:11,160
Xing,

1700
01:01:11,160 --> 01:01:13,240
you said you love walking in gardens

1701
01:01:13,880 --> 01:01:16,640
and watching the greenery sway
in the breeze.

1702
01:01:16,640 --> 01:01:18,920
This afternoon, I went by myself

1703
01:01:18,920 --> 01:01:20,120
to the Dongsiying flower market.

1704
01:01:20,120 --> 01:01:22,400
The air was full of flowers and chatter.

1705
01:01:22,800 --> 01:01:24,160
I wandered around for a long time

1706
01:01:24,160 --> 01:01:25,960
before I finally picked out

1707
01:01:25,960 --> 01:01:27,200
a terrarium.

1708
01:01:27,200 --> 01:01:28,400
(A plant chosen especially
for Wu Xingying)

1709
01:01:28,400 --> 01:01:30,360
It has soft green moss,

1710
01:01:31,400 --> 01:01:33,080
a few delicate plants,

1711
01:01:33,080 --> 01:01:34,760
and a tiny blue stream.

1712
01:01:35,600 --> 01:01:37,440
(Stars in the stream)
Stars seem to float along the water.

1713
01:01:37,440 --> 01:01:39,040
It feels like stepping

1714
01:01:39,040 --> 01:01:40,640
into a quiet little fairy tale.

1715
01:01:41,040 --> 01:01:43,680
It's a tiny world
that fits in your palm.

1716
01:01:44,640 --> 01:01:46,600
But whenever you look at it,

1717
01:01:46,600 --> 01:01:48,000
I hope it reminds you of sunlight

1718
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:49,680
shining through the leaves,

1719
01:01:50,050 --> 01:01:52,160
the little stream we walked by

1720
01:01:52,160 --> 01:01:53,680
that day at the park,

1721
01:01:54,030 --> 01:01:55,520
and the trail beneath the trees.

1722
01:01:56,460 --> 01:01:58,080
(The night before)
Hello.

1723
01:01:58,080 --> 01:01:59,800
Si, um...

1724
01:02:00,120 --> 01:02:01,600
What's this?

1725
01:02:01,600 --> 01:02:03,280
This is for the hospital. You can use it

1726
01:02:03,480 --> 01:02:04,400
to bring her some fruit

1727
01:02:04,400 --> 01:02:06,760
(Insulated lunch box for Wu Xingying)
or food. There's a thermos too.

1728
01:02:06,760 --> 01:02:09,000
And I got these too.

1729
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:10,120
Earplugs

1730
01:02:10,120 --> 01:02:10,800
and a sleep mask,

1731
01:02:10,800 --> 01:02:12,880
in case you guys need to rest
during the day.

1732
01:02:13,200 --> 01:02:14,160
Okay.

1733
01:02:14,160 --> 01:02:15,320
Thanks. I'm sure she'll appreciate it.

1734
01:02:15,320 --> 01:02:15,880
Yeah.

1735
01:02:15,880 --> 01:02:17,520
There's a thermos in there too.

1736
01:02:17,520 --> 01:02:18,600
That's really thoughtful.

1737
01:02:18,600 --> 01:02:19,600
Okay, thanks.

1738
01:02:19,600 --> 01:02:20,800
I'll bring it to her tomorrow.

1739
01:02:21,200 --> 01:02:22,600
Oh, and one more thing.

1740
01:02:22,600 --> 01:02:24,620
(Terrarium)
This is for Xing too.

1741
01:02:24,640 --> 01:02:25,400
That's a lot.

1742
01:02:25,400 --> 01:02:26,520
Here, I'll help you carry it.

1743
01:02:26,520 --> 01:02:26,920
It's okay.

1744
01:02:26,920 --> 01:02:27,600
That's so sweet.

1745
01:02:27,600 --> 01:02:28,800
He really knows
how to take care of someone.

1746
01:02:28,800 --> 01:02:29,800
Since you're stuck

1747
01:02:30,200 --> 01:02:32,400
in the hospital for now,

1748
01:02:32,920 --> 01:02:35,080
I hope this little thing
can keep you company.

1749
01:02:38,840 --> 01:02:40,600
The terrarium is beautiful.

1750
01:02:40,600 --> 01:02:41,480
Thank you.

1751
01:02:41,700 --> 01:02:42,680
(Smiles)

1752
01:02:42,680 --> 01:02:44,680
I'm doing much better today.

1753
01:02:44,680 --> 01:02:45,800
The doctor says I'll soon be able

1754
01:02:45,800 --> 01:02:46,800
to eat and drink again.

1755
01:02:47,800 --> 01:02:49,400
Right now, I've got "Beautiful" playing

1756
01:02:49,400 --> 01:02:50,320
in the background.

1757
01:02:50,520 --> 01:02:51,800
Not sure if you've heard it.

1758
01:02:52,200 --> 01:02:53,480
I just bought a voice recorder.

1759
01:02:53,720 --> 01:02:54,800
If it works,

1760
01:02:54,800 --> 01:02:55,640
you'll be able

1761
01:02:55,640 --> 01:02:56,680
to hear it too.

1762
01:02:59,020 --> 01:03:00,500
(From Wu Xingying's recorder)

1763
01:03:01,360 --> 01:03:02,720
That's so romantic.

1764
01:03:02,720 --> 01:03:04,740
(From Wu Xingying's recorder)

1765
01:03:12,200 --> 01:03:13,760
To me, this song

1766
01:03:13,760 --> 01:03:16,200
feels warm and romantic.

1767
01:03:16,680 --> 01:03:17,880
Why are you so happy?

1768
01:03:18,560 --> 01:03:20,340
(Showing it)
She recorded this for me.

1769
01:03:20,360 --> 01:03:22,560
Oh, it's what she was listening to then.

1770
01:03:24,360 --> 01:03:25,120
That's pretty romantic.

1771
01:03:28,960 --> 01:03:30,080
You should share

1772
01:03:30,080 --> 01:03:31,160
some of your favorite songs with me too.

1773
01:03:31,160 --> 01:03:32,120
Maybe sometime

1774
01:03:32,120 --> 01:03:33,360
we can swap playlists

1775
01:03:33,360 --> 01:03:34,520
and listen to them together.

1776
01:03:36,640 --> 01:03:38,440
I dreamed about you last night.

1777
01:03:38,440 --> 01:03:39,400
When I woke up,

1778
01:03:39,400 --> 01:03:40,320
I still remembered it.

1779
01:03:40,320 --> 01:03:41,480
Now I've forgotten.

1780
01:03:42,720 --> 01:03:44,440
Next time, I guess

1781
01:03:44,440 --> 01:03:45,720
I should write it down
the second I wake up.

1782
01:03:47,880 --> 01:03:49,680
I find myself thinking of you

1783
01:03:49,680 --> 01:03:50,520
in the little moments.

1784
01:03:50,920 --> 01:03:52,320
Like...

1785
01:03:52,320 --> 01:03:54,160
when I'm running alone on the treadmill.

1786
01:03:55,680 --> 01:03:56,520
He really misses her.

1787
01:03:58,800 --> 01:04:00,760
Or when I smell fresh bread
in the morning.

1788
01:04:02,040 --> 01:04:03,160
Where's Sun Bohan?

1789
01:04:04,520 --> 01:04:06,280
You look kind of worn out.

1790
01:04:06,680 --> 01:04:08,400
I said, you look kind of worn out.

1791
01:04:08,400 --> 01:04:09,480
Yeah, a little.

1792
01:04:09,480 --> 01:04:10,280
Honestly,

1793
01:04:11,320 --> 01:04:13,160
I've been pretty worried
over the past few days.

1794
01:04:14,160 --> 01:04:16,480
I promised Xing

1795
01:04:16,480 --> 01:04:19,080
that while she's away,

1796
01:04:19,080 --> 01:04:19,840
I'd...

1797
01:04:19,840 --> 01:04:21,160
record things for her

1798
01:04:21,160 --> 01:04:22,880
so it'd feel like

1799
01:04:22,880 --> 01:04:24,120
she was still here with us.

1800
01:04:24,660 --> 01:04:26,800
(I'll record it while you're away)
I hope you get plenty of rest.

1801
01:04:26,800 --> 01:04:27,840
The house

1802
01:04:28,120 --> 01:04:28,840
and I

1803
01:04:29,280 --> 01:04:29,920
will both be here.

1804
01:04:33,520 --> 01:04:35,380
(I'll record it while you're away)
Three, two...

1805
01:04:38,040 --> 01:04:39,440
So handsome!

1806
01:04:39,440 --> 01:04:40,600
Let's take a picture.

1807
01:04:40,600 --> 01:04:41,520
Okay, come on.

1808
01:04:41,760 --> 01:04:42,560
I'll hold this.

1809
01:04:42,560 --> 01:04:42,960
Twinkle Twinkle.

1810
01:04:42,960 --> 01:04:43,600
Yeah, perfect.

1811
01:04:43,600 --> 01:04:44,680
Xing.

1812
01:04:48,020 --> 01:04:48,560
That's kind of magical.

1813
01:04:48,560 --> 01:04:49,200
Nice.

1814
01:04:49,200 --> 01:04:50,760
I'm holding two star lights,

1815
01:04:50,760 --> 01:04:51,920
one in each hand.

1816
01:04:51,920 --> 01:04:53,640
It almost feels like you're here
with me.

1817
01:05:04,320 --> 01:05:06,600
I saw your rock-climbing photos.

1818
01:05:07,200 --> 01:05:08,960
You looked like a pro.

1819
01:05:08,960 --> 01:05:10,520
I really wish I could've gone with you.

1820
01:05:10,720 --> 01:05:12,040
(Laughs)
Too bad

1821
01:05:12,040 --> 01:05:13,920
I didn't get to see you climb in person,

1822
01:05:14,320 --> 01:05:16,240
but I'll keep these photos forever.

1823
01:05:16,380 --> 01:05:18,500
(Happy)

1824
01:05:18,520 --> 01:05:19,840
Look at that smile.

1825
01:05:22,440 --> 01:05:24,680
(Bohan at the flower shop)
In the second photo, you hold a plant.

1826
01:05:24,920 --> 01:05:27,200
Now I'm holding one too.

1827
01:05:27,200 --> 01:05:28,720
It's like we're in parallel worlds.

1828
01:05:30,600 --> 01:05:32,360
Seeing your photo made me so happy.

1829
01:05:32,360 --> 01:05:33,600
Don't forget to eat.

1830
01:05:34,360 --> 01:05:35,440
Wait for me to come back.

1831
01:05:36,920 --> 01:05:39,760
Take care of yourself
and stay happy while I'm away.

1832
01:05:48,040 --> 01:05:49,240
Sun Bohan's heart

1833
01:05:49,240 --> 01:05:50,440
must be so full right now.

1834
01:05:51,520 --> 01:05:52,400
Completely full.

1835
01:06:24,440 --> 01:06:25,280
He's writing back.

1836
01:06:28,480 --> 01:06:29,400
Xing,

1837
01:06:29,880 --> 01:06:31,680
I got your voice recorder.

1838
01:06:31,680 --> 01:06:33,680
I listened to "Beautiful",
the song you shared.

1839
01:06:34,480 --> 01:06:35,680
I'd heard it before.

1840
01:06:36,160 --> 01:06:37,760
It feels like early spring,

1841
01:06:37,760 --> 01:06:39,280
a blanket warmed by the sun.

1842
01:06:39,680 --> 01:06:40,800
Soft and cozy.

1843
01:06:41,560 --> 01:06:43,880
I listened to it three times
on the couch.

1844
01:06:44,920 --> 01:06:47,440
It felt like you were sitting
next to me.

1845
01:06:47,960 --> 01:06:49,520
I heard you're doing better.

1846
01:06:49,520 --> 01:06:50,520
That made me really happy.

1847
01:06:52,840 --> 01:06:55,040
Si and Cui Yihang
went to the stargazing room.

1848
01:06:55,480 --> 01:06:57,680
They looked so happy together.

1849
01:07:07,440 --> 01:07:08,640
He's not going to cry, is he?

1850
01:07:15,520 --> 01:07:17,840
So hurry up and get better.

1851
01:07:17,840 --> 01:07:19,360
Once you're out of the hospital,

1852
01:07:19,360 --> 01:07:21,000
I want us to go
to the stargazing room together.

1853
01:07:23,960 --> 01:07:25,840
I'm also sending a photo

1854
01:07:25,840 --> 01:07:26,760
of me with your letter.

1855
01:07:27,080 --> 01:07:28,560
Today's weather was stunning,

1856
01:07:28,760 --> 01:07:31,240
especially at sunset.

1857
01:07:31,680 --> 01:07:32,840
So I wanted to share

1858
01:07:32,840 --> 01:07:34,160
that moment with you.

1859
01:07:34,760 --> 01:07:35,440
From Sun Bohan.

1860
01:07:43,600 --> 01:07:45,320
This is so sweet and romantic.

1861
01:07:59,800 --> 01:08:01,000
It's beautiful, isn't it?

1862
01:08:01,000 --> 01:08:01,760
Yeah.

1863
01:08:03,400 --> 01:08:04,560
I can't believe this guy

1864
01:08:04,560 --> 01:08:05,200
keeps making me cry.

1865
01:08:05,200 --> 01:08:06,160
He's full of surprises.

1866
01:08:06,160 --> 01:08:07,440
He looks like

1867
01:08:07,440 --> 01:08:08,320
this big, tough guy,

1868
01:08:08,320 --> 01:08:10,200
but he's actually so thoughtful.

1869
01:08:11,120 --> 01:08:12,000
Yeah, really thoughtful.

1870
01:08:12,480 --> 01:08:13,920
This is the kind of thing

1871
01:08:13,920 --> 01:08:14,920
that can only happen

1872
01:08:14,920 --> 01:08:15,480
in a place

1873
01:08:15,480 --> 01:08:17,280
like the Signal House.

1874
01:08:17,280 --> 01:08:17,960
It's so heartwarming.

1875
01:08:17,960 --> 01:08:19,760
(Such a warm group)
This season's Signal House

1876
01:08:19,760 --> 01:08:20,360
is honestly

1877
01:08:21,080 --> 01:08:22,960
so warm and comforting.

1878
01:08:23,360 --> 01:08:24,880
Everyone's so open

1879
01:08:24,880 --> 01:08:25,680
and sincere about their feelings.

1880
01:08:25,680 --> 01:08:27,560
Why write letters?

1881
01:08:28,040 --> 01:08:28,760
Because

1882
01:08:28,760 --> 01:08:30,000
with handwriting,

1883
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:31,320
you can feel

1884
01:08:31,480 --> 01:08:32,800
the emotion in every stroke.

1885
01:08:32,800 --> 01:08:33,960
Every word reflects

1886
01:08:33,960 --> 01:08:34,920
what you were feeling

1887
01:08:34,920 --> 01:08:35,960
when you wrote it.

1888
01:08:36,200 --> 01:08:38,400
You may not see the person

1889
01:08:38,400 --> 01:08:40,760
or hear their voice,

1890
01:08:40,760 --> 01:08:42,120
but you can still feel them

1891
01:08:42,120 --> 01:08:43,640
in the way they write.

1892
01:08:43,640 --> 01:08:45,280
You can feel their longing
in every stroke.

1893
01:08:56,360 --> 01:08:57,480
What's going on?

1894
01:08:58,100 --> 01:08:59,100
(Gets up)

1895
01:09:00,120 --> 01:09:01,520
Why isn't she back yet?

1896
01:09:06,140 --> 01:09:08,500
(Peeks out)

1897
01:09:09,400 --> 01:09:10,560
Our letter writer.

1898
01:09:11,660 --> 01:09:13,620
(Leaves)

1899
01:09:17,760 --> 01:09:18,480
Still playing?

1900
01:09:18,480 --> 01:09:19,600
Yes.

1901
01:09:19,600 --> 01:09:20,800
Nice.

1902
01:09:21,520 --> 01:09:22,840
Meng and Liang Xiaoyu.

1903
01:09:23,300 --> 01:09:26,620
(Turns back)

1904
01:09:37,960 --> 01:09:39,280
Is he waiting for Sha Yue'er?

1905
01:09:39,840 --> 01:09:41,080
He must be waiting for her.

1906
01:09:43,620 --> 01:09:47,100
(Heads to the gym)

1907
01:09:53,940 --> 01:09:58,900
(Looks outside)

1908
01:09:58,920 --> 01:10:00,080
This was where he and Sha Yue'er

1909
01:10:00,080 --> 01:10:01,160
had their first little secret spot.

1910
01:10:16,700 --> 01:10:20,900
(Looks toward the door)

1911
01:10:23,260 --> 01:10:28,020
(Looks at the card)

1912
01:10:35,960 --> 01:10:36,240
It's okay.

1913
01:10:36,240 --> 01:10:37,800
We'll handle the rest.

1914
01:10:39,040 --> 01:10:41,640
Thanks, guys.

1915
01:10:41,640 --> 01:10:45,040
You two work harder
than anyone in the world.

1916
01:10:45,520 --> 01:10:47,120
Hardest-working duo in the house.

1917
01:10:47,560 --> 01:10:48,960
No, I mean in the world.

1918
01:10:49,160 --> 01:10:50,400
Let me turn one over for you.

1919
01:10:51,040 --> 01:10:51,920
Wait.

1920
01:10:51,920 --> 01:10:52,680
No.

1921
01:10:53,960 --> 01:10:55,000
Your hair's a mess.

1922
01:10:58,360 --> 01:10:59,480
We'll head out first.

1923
01:10:59,760 --> 01:11:00,440
Go ahead. It's fine.

1924
01:11:00,440 --> 01:11:01,760
Grab some for breakfast.

1925
01:11:03,540 --> 01:11:05,100
(Puts it down)

1926
01:11:05,220 --> 01:11:06,380
(Takes it)

1927
01:11:11,360 --> 01:11:13,040
I never ate my bread from yesterday.

1928
01:11:14,320 --> 01:11:15,920
I totally forgot about it.

1929
01:11:16,160 --> 01:11:17,800
So you skipped breakfast today?

1930
01:11:18,360 --> 01:11:19,760
Lately, when I wake up,

1931
01:11:19,760 --> 01:11:21,360
I feel like I've...

1932
01:11:22,180 --> 01:11:23,820
(Tilts head)

1933
01:11:23,840 --> 01:11:25,880
aged 20 years overnight.

1934
01:11:27,920 --> 01:11:29,400
Honestly, it feels like even more.

1935
01:11:29,400 --> 01:11:31,480
It's getting harder
to wake up every day.

1936
01:11:33,200 --> 01:11:34,200
I feel like that scent

1937
01:11:34,200 --> 01:11:35,880
makes me sleep really deeply.

1938
01:11:39,520 --> 01:11:40,360
Really?

1939
01:11:40,360 --> 01:11:41,120
It actually works?

1940
01:11:42,240 --> 01:11:42,920
Sweet dreams.

1941
01:11:43,400 --> 01:11:44,800
Good. As long as it works.

1942
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:46,720
Here.

1943
01:11:46,720 --> 01:11:47,480
I'll do it.

1944
01:11:47,980 --> 01:11:49,060
(Pulls her hands back)

1945
01:11:50,420 --> 01:11:53,100
(Follows)

1946
01:11:54,260 --> 01:11:58,140
(Follows)

1947
01:11:58,920 --> 01:12:00,360
It's like there's an invisible string
between them.

1948
01:12:01,920 --> 01:12:03,160
Yeah, this one's clean.

1949
01:12:04,080 --> 01:12:05,000
Here, put it down.

1950
01:12:07,000 --> 01:12:07,840
Look at that teamwork.

1951
01:12:08,700 --> 01:12:10,940
(One washes, one dries)

1952
01:12:10,960 --> 01:12:11,760
Perfect.

1953
01:12:14,000 --> 01:12:14,880
So cute.

1954
01:12:16,280 --> 01:12:17,560
Okay.

1955
01:12:18,920 --> 01:12:19,160
Here.

1956
01:12:19,160 --> 01:12:20,000
Thanks for the help.

1957
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:21,640
You did all the hard work.

1958
01:12:22,080 --> 01:12:23,160
You washed everything.

1959
01:12:26,400 --> 01:12:27,200
Let's go.

1960
01:12:28,360 --> 01:12:29,760
They forgot their photo.

1961
01:12:35,920 --> 01:12:36,720
Fang.

1962
01:12:38,920 --> 01:12:40,120
Were you calling me?

1963
01:12:41,080 --> 01:12:42,000
I forgot my photo.

1964
01:12:42,520 --> 01:12:43,320
Thanks.

1965
01:12:43,320 --> 01:12:44,560
No problem.

1966
01:12:44,560 --> 01:12:46,560
Thanks.

1967
01:12:50,400 --> 01:12:51,080
What's this?

1968
01:12:53,840 --> 01:12:54,920
What's that light out there?

1969
01:12:54,920 --> 01:12:55,680
Any idea?

1970
01:12:56,560 --> 01:12:57,520
The stargazing room.

1971
01:12:57,520 --> 01:12:58,290
Whoa.

1972
01:13:00,400 --> 01:13:00,960
Careful.

1973
01:13:00,960 --> 01:13:01,960
That breaks really easily.

1974
01:13:04,160 --> 01:13:06,480
Is that a gift for you?

1975
01:13:06,480 --> 01:13:08,360
It's a terrarium

1976
01:13:08,360 --> 01:13:11,000
I gave him.

1977
01:13:14,200 --> 01:13:15,440
Is it for fish?

1978
01:13:16,240 --> 01:13:16,760
You...

1979
01:13:16,760 --> 01:13:17,880
For fish?

1980
01:13:22,160 --> 01:13:23,600
I thought it was with me.

1981
01:13:23,600 --> 01:13:25,140
(Hands it over)
I even looked through it.

1982
01:13:26,040 --> 01:13:27,720
Three, two, one.

1983
01:13:28,840 --> 01:13:30,000
Thanks.

1984
01:13:31,190 --> 01:13:32,140
Let's warm it up a bit.

1985
01:13:34,320 --> 01:13:35,600
Where should I put the bottle?

1986
01:13:36,120 --> 01:13:37,120
Here.

1987
01:13:37,860 --> 01:13:39,900
(Tucks it in)

1988
01:13:45,480 --> 01:13:47,000
Sha Yue'er still isn't back?

1989
01:13:47,520 --> 01:13:48,720
So they don't know.

1990
01:13:48,720 --> 01:13:50,320
Yeah, she's not back yet.

1991
01:13:52,600 --> 01:13:53,480
Cao Yiheng,

1992
01:13:53,480 --> 01:13:54,320
who lit that up outside?

1993
01:13:54,320 --> 01:13:54,880
Who used the coin?

1994
01:13:55,600 --> 01:13:56,280
Wasn't it Cui Yihang?

1995
01:13:57,200 --> 01:13:57,760
No, not Cui Yihang.

1996
01:13:57,760 --> 01:13:58,600
I asked him.

1997
01:13:59,000 --> 01:14:00,400
Wasn't he in the stargazing room?

1998
01:14:01,080 --> 01:14:02,040
I asked him.

1999
01:14:02,040 --> 01:14:04,080
I ran into him on my way in.

2000
01:14:04,080 --> 01:14:04,400
I mean...

2001
01:14:04,400 --> 01:14:05,680
I saw him on the stairs.

2002
01:14:05,680 --> 01:14:06,920
I asked if that was him.

2003
01:14:06,920 --> 01:14:07,840
He said no.

2004
01:14:07,840 --> 01:14:08,200
And then...

2005
01:14:08,200 --> 01:14:09,360
Maybe he's messing with you.

2006
01:14:09,960 --> 01:14:10,720
She doesn't know.

2007
01:14:12,720 --> 01:14:13,800
Let's go.

2008
01:14:15,760 --> 01:14:16,480
He even asked me

2009
01:14:16,480 --> 01:14:17,720
why it was lit up.

2010
01:14:17,720 --> 01:14:18,800
I told him that someone...

2011
01:14:18,800 --> 01:14:20,200
Obviously, someone must've done it.

2012
01:14:25,740 --> 01:14:28,140
(Gets up)

2013
01:14:29,000 --> 01:14:29,960
Chen Hewen and Sha Yue'er

2014
01:14:29,960 --> 01:14:30,680
didn't go out together, did they?

2015
01:14:31,480 --> 01:14:32,360
It's possible.

2016
01:14:32,680 --> 01:14:33,480
Called it.

2017
01:14:33,920 --> 01:14:35,280
But... wouldn't Cui Kaiyi

2018
01:14:35,280 --> 01:14:36,160
know about it?

2019
01:14:36,160 --> 01:14:36,680
Right?

2020
01:14:37,800 --> 01:14:39,120
Then maybe it's not them.

2021
01:14:39,120 --> 01:14:40,720
I don't know.

2022
01:14:43,840 --> 01:14:45,280
I'll grab the sheet music.

2023
01:14:45,280 --> 01:14:45,920
Okay.

2024
01:14:54,080 --> 01:14:55,880
Let me put the membrane on my flute.

2025
01:15:00,200 --> 01:15:01,480
- A flute.
- Han Xiangzi.

2026
01:15:05,960 --> 01:15:07,560
Having the sheet music really helps.

2027
01:15:08,040 --> 01:15:08,960
Yeah, definitely.

2028
01:15:09,200 --> 01:15:10,200
You two are on the same page too.

2029
01:15:21,960 --> 01:15:23,320
Let's play something together.

2030
01:15:23,600 --> 01:15:24,960
Want to take a look?

2031
01:15:24,960 --> 01:15:25,840
What can you play?

2032
01:15:26,280 --> 01:15:27,280
What can I play?

2033
01:15:27,280 --> 01:15:28,280
This one.

2034
01:15:28,280 --> 01:15:28,640
Okay.

2035
01:15:30,040 --> 01:15:31,560
You can play this just by reading it?

2036
01:15:34,380 --> 01:15:36,180
(Totally impressed)

2037
01:15:36,200 --> 01:15:37,240
I can.

2038
01:15:37,240 --> 01:15:37,920
Anytime.

2039
01:15:39,680 --> 01:15:40,720
It's in C major.

2040
01:15:40,720 --> 01:15:41,960
Okay, that's talent.

2041
01:15:41,960 --> 01:15:42,800
Where do we start?

2042
01:15:48,360 --> 01:15:49,040
From the top.

2043
01:15:49,600 --> 01:15:50,120
Let's try again.

2044
01:15:50,120 --> 01:15:50,960
Okay, got it.

2045
01:15:51,280 --> 01:15:52,720
Five, six, seven, go.

2046
01:15:56,080 --> 01:15:56,880
East meets West.

2047
01:15:59,680 --> 01:16:01,520
It's "I Only Care About You".

2048
01:16:01,520 --> 01:16:02,480
Yeah.

2049
01:16:03,880 --> 01:16:05,280
That actually works.

2050
01:16:05,280 --> 01:16:06,240
They just work with everything.

2051
01:16:06,240 --> 01:16:07,110
Whoa.

2052
01:16:09,280 --> 01:16:11,360
Is this the Signal House anthem now?

2053
01:16:11,720 --> 01:16:12,720
That's impressive.

2054
01:16:23,820 --> 01:16:25,180
(Stops)

2055
01:16:28,900 --> 01:16:29,940
(Stops with her)

2056
01:16:30,480 --> 01:16:31,120
This sounds...

2057
01:16:31,120 --> 01:16:32,680
Is it the guitar or me?

2058
01:16:32,680 --> 01:16:33,440
It sounds

2059
01:16:33,440 --> 01:16:34,440
really stiff.

2060
01:16:35,320 --> 01:16:36,200
Definitely the guitar.

2061
01:16:38,120 --> 01:16:38,960
Definitely the guitar.

2062
01:16:39,120 --> 01:16:40,350
(Definitely the guitar)
Yu Yang.

2063
01:16:41,480 --> 01:16:43,280
(Laughs)
Thanks.

2064
01:16:43,280 --> 01:16:44,280
It's actually me.

2065
01:16:45,080 --> 01:16:45,800
Now she's happy.

2066
01:16:47,880 --> 01:16:50,400
YuLiang Never Fades.

2067
01:16:50,400 --> 01:16:51,520
They're really in sync.

2068
01:16:53,560 --> 01:16:55,160
This is nice.

2069
01:16:55,360 --> 01:16:55,920
Have a seat.

2070
01:16:55,920 --> 01:16:57,320
Okay, time to enjoy the show.

2071
01:16:59,240 --> 01:17:00,560
Let's warm up a little.

2072
01:17:02,000 --> 01:17:03,280
Now it's a whole concert.

2073
01:17:03,800 --> 01:17:05,480
Can you play that one?

2074
01:17:05,920 --> 01:17:06,480
Which one?

2075
01:17:06,480 --> 01:17:09,240
The one from "The Legend
of the White Snake".

2076
01:17:09,440 --> 01:17:10,320
What's it called again?

2077
01:17:10,320 --> 01:17:11,400
I forgot too.

2078
01:17:11,400 --> 01:17:12,160
Hum it, and I can play it.

2079
01:17:12,160 --> 01:17:14,040
♪Bai Suzhen from Mount Qingcheng♪

2080
01:17:14,040 --> 01:17:14,720
This one?

2081
01:17:14,720 --> 01:17:15,080
Yeah.

2082
01:17:17,340 --> 01:17:20,100
(Plays it effortlessly)

2083
01:17:20,120 --> 01:17:21,360
That sounds so good.

2084
01:17:28,520 --> 01:17:29,040
Honestly...

2085
01:17:29,040 --> 01:17:29,400
I like it.

2086
01:17:29,400 --> 01:17:31,240
Talent is such a plus.

2087
01:17:31,560 --> 01:17:32,360
Nice.

2088
01:17:32,640 --> 01:17:34,280
Go play it on the boat.

2089
01:17:36,560 --> 01:17:37,760
I'll film you.

2090
01:17:37,920 --> 01:17:38,900
Let's go.

2091
01:17:40,080 --> 01:17:41,200
Go!

2092
01:17:42,000 --> 01:17:43,320
You have to stand, okay?

2093
01:17:43,320 --> 01:17:44,520
Play it standing up,

2094
01:17:45,040 --> 01:17:46,360
and I'll row alongside you.

2095
01:17:46,600 --> 01:17:47,960
You know...

2096
01:17:47,960 --> 01:17:48,920
Then you'll tip over in seconds.

2097
01:17:48,920 --> 01:17:50,440
And there he goes.

2098
01:17:53,040 --> 01:17:54,560
You printed all this sheet music?

2099
01:17:55,280 --> 01:17:55,800
Yeah.

2100
01:17:55,800 --> 01:17:56,960
You really are the music crew.

2101
01:17:56,960 --> 01:17:57,760
Welcome.

2102
01:17:57,760 --> 01:17:58,520
The music crew.

2103
01:17:58,520 --> 01:18:00,280
What else should we play?

2104
01:18:00,760 --> 01:18:01,920
We can request songs?

2105
01:18:03,480 --> 01:18:04,480
Requests are open.

2106
01:18:04,760 --> 01:18:05,320
Over there.

2107
01:18:07,960 --> 01:18:09,080
She's tired.

2108
01:18:09,320 --> 01:18:10,560
You're completely spent.

2109
01:18:14,240 --> 01:18:15,360
Sing a little.

2110
01:18:15,360 --> 01:18:17,080
Yu Yang, I'll back you up.

2111
01:18:18,800 --> 01:18:21,810
♪Time keeps rushing by♪

2112
01:18:21,810 --> 01:18:24,220
♪You're all I care about♪

2113
01:18:26,190 --> 01:18:31,310
♪I'd gladly breathe you in♪

2114
01:18:32,520 --> 01:18:38,230
♪How often do we find someone
who truly knows us?♪

2115
01:18:38,240 --> 01:18:39,070
They're incredible.

2116
01:18:39,070 --> 01:18:41,390
♪I'd give up even the strength to live♪

2117
01:18:41,520 --> 01:18:43,320
Some are happy. Some are not so much.

2118
01:18:44,870 --> 01:18:48,270
♪So I'm begging you♪

2119
01:18:48,590 --> 01:18:51,850
♪Don't let me leave you♪

2120
01:18:53,360 --> 01:18:56,340
♪Without you, I can't feel♪

2121
01:18:56,340 --> 01:18:58,770
♪even the slightest bit of love♪

2122
01:19:21,180 --> 01:19:23,580
(Slips it into his pocket)

2123
01:19:27,900 --> 01:19:29,820
(Looks)

2124
01:19:31,380 --> 01:19:33,580
(Looks again)

2125
01:19:50,400 --> 01:19:51,040
Zhao Xilun.

2126
01:19:51,480 --> 01:19:52,520
What are you doing?

2127
01:19:52,520 --> 01:19:53,760
I was thinking,

2128
01:19:53,760 --> 01:19:54,840
what if those two went out together?

2129
01:19:54,840 --> 01:19:56,800
Which two? Chen Hewen?

2130
01:19:56,800 --> 01:19:58,120
Chen Hewen and Sha Yue'er?

2131
01:19:58,360 --> 01:19:59,320
Is Chen Hewen back?

2132
01:20:00,280 --> 01:20:01,320
Neither of them is back.

2133
01:20:02,600 --> 01:20:04,200
And it's already this late.

2134
01:20:05,400 --> 01:20:06,120
No way.

2135
01:20:08,400 --> 01:20:10,280
But it's possible, right?

2136
01:20:11,120 --> 01:20:11,880
Yeah.

2137
01:20:12,320 --> 01:20:13,280
So now I'm...

2138
01:20:14,680 --> 01:20:15,560
Don't spiral,

2139
01:20:15,560 --> 01:20:16,080
okay?

2140
01:20:16,080 --> 01:20:16,600
I know.

2141
01:20:16,600 --> 01:20:17,920
I just feel like...

2142
01:20:19,740 --> 01:20:22,180
(Sighs)

2143
01:20:25,720 --> 01:20:26,760
I don't know if..

2144
01:20:27,440 --> 01:20:29,640
Should I still... You know?

2145
01:20:29,640 --> 01:20:30,180
(Takes out the card)

2146
01:20:30,760 --> 01:20:31,960
Is that for the stargazing room?

2147
01:20:31,960 --> 01:20:33,240
I figured I'd leave it here for now.

2148
01:20:33,240 --> 01:20:33,660
(Puts it down)

2149
01:20:35,560 --> 01:20:36,960
Just wait. No rush.

2150
01:20:36,960 --> 01:20:37,840
You care, so you're overthinking it.

2151
01:20:38,480 --> 01:20:38,880
Yeah.

2152
01:20:39,200 --> 01:20:40,360
Come on.

2153
01:20:42,320 --> 01:20:43,800
Let's go boating.

2154
01:20:43,880 --> 01:20:44,960
Let's take the boat out.

2155
01:20:45,760 --> 01:20:46,760
And after that,

2156
01:20:46,760 --> 01:20:48,520
we can get a massage or something.

2157
01:20:48,520 --> 01:20:49,560
Yeah, sounds good.

2158
01:20:49,560 --> 01:20:50,880
We know how to treat ourselves.

2159
01:20:50,880 --> 01:20:51,640
We sure do.

2160
01:20:54,240 --> 01:20:55,520
The boat lights up.

2161
01:20:55,620 --> 01:20:57,280
(Lights under the boat)

2162
01:20:57,280 --> 01:20:58,640
It wasn't like that before, was it?

2163
01:20:58,640 --> 01:21:00,520
Now we even get lights.

2164
01:21:03,720 --> 01:21:04,760
I'll teach you how to row.

2165
01:21:05,560 --> 01:21:06,760
I've done this twice.

2166
01:21:08,200 --> 01:21:09,780
Boat King.

2167
01:21:09,800 --> 01:21:10,560
Boat King.

2168
01:21:12,800 --> 01:21:13,840
I'll show you how it's done.

2169
01:21:14,560 --> 01:21:15,240
Whoa, there are flowers too.

2170
01:21:15,720 --> 01:21:16,800
Flowers?

2171
01:21:16,800 --> 01:21:18,360
(Flowers)
Those weren't here before.

2172
01:21:18,360 --> 01:21:19,480
Look at us...

2173
01:21:19,840 --> 01:21:21,400
How is that even fair?

2174
01:21:21,400 --> 01:21:22,200
Seriously.

2175
01:21:23,680 --> 01:21:25,600
This is way more romantic
than my last ride.

2176
01:21:28,160 --> 01:21:29,240
I can't.

2177
01:21:30,120 --> 01:21:31,040
That's how I earned

2178
01:21:31,040 --> 01:21:32,320
the title of Boat King.

2179
01:21:32,320 --> 01:21:33,760
Okay, let's set sail.

2180
01:21:34,040 --> 01:21:34,960
Boatman.

2181
01:21:37,600 --> 01:21:38,400
This is nice.

2182
01:21:40,960 --> 01:21:41,870
Oh my God.

2183
01:21:42,680 --> 01:21:45,440
This feels amazing.

2184
01:21:46,920 --> 01:21:48,480
You weren't this excited on your date.

2185
01:21:48,480 --> 01:21:50,000
What's gotten into you now?

2186
01:21:53,360 --> 01:21:54,080
Look.

2187
01:21:54,440 --> 01:21:55,400
The stargazing room's pretty nice.

2188
01:21:55,400 --> 01:21:55,960
Have you been?

2189
01:22:02,880 --> 01:22:03,400
Nope.

2190
01:22:03,400 --> 01:22:04,640
Who would I go with?

2191
01:22:05,840 --> 01:22:06,640
Look at those two.

2192
01:22:07,960 --> 01:22:08,960
Hello.

2193
01:22:10,760 --> 01:22:11,560
Can they see us?

2194
01:22:11,560 --> 01:22:12,760
Hi!

2195
01:22:15,680 --> 01:22:16,760
He's been waiting forever.

2196
01:22:20,580 --> 01:22:23,420
(Notices him)

2197
01:22:24,060 --> 01:22:26,740
(Deflated)

2198
01:22:29,760 --> 01:22:30,840
Are we seriously the clowns here?

2199
01:22:30,840 --> 01:22:31,680
They're in the stargazing room,

2200
01:22:31,680 --> 01:22:32,680
and we're out here...

2201
01:22:33,060 --> 01:22:34,240
(Laughs)

2202
01:22:34,240 --> 01:22:35,320
It's not my first time

2203
01:22:35,320 --> 01:22:36,280
being the clown.

2204
01:22:36,760 --> 01:22:37,880
I always end up being one.

2205
01:22:41,960 --> 01:22:43,280
If they're still not back this late,

2206
01:22:43,640 --> 01:22:45,280
they probably went into the city.

2207
01:22:49,200 --> 01:22:50,200
Right?

2208
01:22:53,080 --> 01:22:54,040
Should I still give it to her?

2209
01:22:54,040 --> 01:22:55,400
Now he's having second thoughts.

2210
01:22:56,160 --> 01:22:57,160
Didn't you already...

2211
01:22:57,920 --> 01:22:59,600
I did,
but I haven't given her the card.

2212
01:22:59,600 --> 01:23:01,360
Maybe I just shouldn't.

2213
01:23:03,080 --> 01:23:04,600
It'd be so awkward.

2214
01:23:07,120 --> 01:23:07,600
Right?

2215
01:23:09,080 --> 01:23:10,320
Why would it be awkward?

2216
01:23:15,640 --> 01:23:16,560
It just would.

2217
01:23:17,280 --> 01:23:17,880
You know?

2218
01:23:20,080 --> 01:23:22,600
Then don't do it
if it doesn't feel right.

2219
01:23:22,600 --> 01:23:23,320
Yeah.

2220
01:23:23,720 --> 01:23:24,120
If you...

2221
01:23:24,120 --> 01:23:24,680
The thing is,

2222
01:23:24,680 --> 01:23:25,640
if you're already

2223
01:23:25,640 --> 01:23:26,520
this unsure

2224
01:23:26,960 --> 01:23:27,720
and you still go in,

2225
01:23:27,720 --> 01:23:28,760
you're not going

2226
01:23:28,760 --> 01:23:29,480
to enjoy it

2227
01:23:29,480 --> 01:23:30,560
or feel good about it.

2228
01:23:30,560 --> 01:23:30,880
Yeah.

2229
01:23:30,880 --> 01:23:32,480
It'll just keep bothering you.

2230
01:23:32,480 --> 01:23:35,080
So don't force it.

2231
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:37,560
I think you should just

2232
01:23:37,560 --> 01:23:38,640
wait a day or two.

2233
01:23:38,640 --> 01:23:40,040
Spend more time together.

2234
01:23:40,040 --> 01:23:41,520
If you stop feeling so unsure,

2235
01:23:41,520 --> 01:23:42,320
then give her the card.

2236
01:23:42,320 --> 01:23:43,520
You still have time.

2237
01:23:49,480 --> 01:23:50,600
What's meant to come will come.

2238
01:23:50,600 --> 01:23:52,320
What's meant to go, you can't hold onto.

2239
01:23:52,320 --> 01:23:54,200
If it's yours,
it'll find its way to you.

2240
01:23:54,200 --> 01:23:54,640
If not, let it go.

2241
01:23:54,640 --> 01:23:56,040
You know that lyric?

2242
01:23:56,320 --> 01:23:56,760
Whose?

2243
01:23:56,760 --> 01:23:57,720
What's meant to come will come.

2244
01:23:57,720 --> 01:23:59,280
What's meant to go, you can't hold onto.

2245
01:23:59,280 --> 01:24:00,720
Nope. Never heard it.

2246
01:24:02,160 --> 01:24:04,720
♪Letting go♪

2247
01:24:04,720 --> 01:24:07,760
♪I can finally let you go♪

2248
01:24:08,960 --> 01:24:09,840
They're on a date.

2249
01:24:10,760 --> 01:24:11,760
They're on a date.

2250
01:24:11,760 --> 01:24:12,320
Keep it down.

2251
01:24:12,940 --> 01:24:13,840
(Waves)

2252
01:24:13,840 --> 01:24:15,200
They're actually waving
for them to stop.

2253
01:24:15,680 --> 01:24:17,040
Stop singing!

2254
01:24:17,040 --> 01:24:17,840
Third wheel.

2255
01:24:17,840 --> 01:24:18,840
Clown.

2256
01:24:18,840 --> 01:24:20,000
You think they're waving hello,

2257
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:20,360
but actually

2258
01:24:20,360 --> 01:24:22,560
they're telling them to go away.

2259
01:24:23,260 --> 01:24:24,700
(Waves)

2260
01:24:24,720 --> 01:24:25,720
Go away!

2261
01:24:25,720 --> 01:24:27,200
(Waves)
We're busy over here!

2262
01:24:28,680 --> 01:24:30,000
Clown.

2263
01:24:30,440 --> 01:24:31,880
Full-on clown mode.

2264
01:24:32,640 --> 01:24:33,640
Sorry.

2265
01:24:33,640 --> 01:24:35,600
It just feels great singing out here.

2266
01:24:35,600 --> 01:24:37,000
I used to imitate

2267
01:24:37,000 --> 01:24:38,280
Li Ronghao and Joker Xue.

2268
01:24:38,280 --> 01:24:38,720
I'm serious.

2269
01:24:38,720 --> 01:24:39,800
Joker Xue is pretty easy to imitate.

2270
01:24:39,800 --> 01:24:43,760
♪This is where our love should end♪

2271
01:24:45,480 --> 01:24:46,280
Li Ronghao.

2272
01:24:46,940 --> 01:24:49,380
(Really getting into it)

2273
01:24:49,400 --> 01:24:51,160
You two out here on this pond...

2274
01:24:51,880 --> 01:24:54,840
♪Drifting farther and farther away♪

2275
01:24:54,840 --> 01:24:55,800
That actually sounds like him.

2276
01:24:57,720 --> 01:25:01,680
♪I guess I'll accept it♪

2277
01:25:01,680 --> 01:25:03,600
♪But all you gave me♪

2278
01:25:04,520 --> 01:25:07,760
♪was a goodbye♪

2279
01:25:09,080 --> 01:25:10,960
A goodbye!

2280
01:25:13,240 --> 01:25:14,320
Want to go up there?

2281
01:25:14,320 --> 01:25:15,240
Sure.

2282
01:25:17,000 --> 01:25:18,720
Want to try the swing?

2283
01:25:18,880 --> 01:25:19,960
He's done it before.

2284
01:25:20,360 --> 01:25:21,320
Let's swing together.

2285
01:25:21,560 --> 01:25:22,680
Like this?

2286
01:25:22,680 --> 01:25:23,280
Yeah.

2287
01:25:23,680 --> 01:25:24,760
Again?

2288
01:25:25,360 --> 01:25:27,560
He's getting everyone to do this.

2289
01:25:27,800 --> 01:25:29,520
Wait, how do we get it going?

2290
01:25:30,520 --> 01:25:31,760
Like a crab.

2291
01:25:33,580 --> 01:25:35,020
(Uses both feet to get the swing moving)

2292
01:25:38,360 --> 01:25:40,080
We just sway side to side

2293
01:25:40,080 --> 01:25:41,160
and push off the ground.

2294
01:25:42,280 --> 01:25:43,760
We look like we're running.

2295
01:25:44,120 --> 01:25:44,760
I am running.

2296
01:25:44,760 --> 01:25:46,000
That's what it feels like.

2297
01:25:46,600 --> 01:25:48,760
(Pushes off)
It's tough when you're 190cm.

2298
01:25:49,380 --> 01:25:50,940
(Happy)

2299
01:25:50,960 --> 01:25:51,960
Then push like this.

2300
01:25:53,280 --> 01:25:54,960
They look like two gorillas now.

2301
01:25:54,960 --> 01:25:55,840
They kind of do.

2302
01:25:56,080 --> 01:25:57,560
My legs are getting stiff.

2303
01:25:57,560 --> 01:25:58,800
Maybe we should stop.

2304
01:26:01,200 --> 01:26:01,880
This one swing

2305
01:26:01,880 --> 01:26:03,680
has unlocked so many...

2306
01:26:03,680 --> 01:26:04,440
new modes for us.

2307
01:26:05,880 --> 01:26:07,360
Why are guys like this?

2308
01:26:08,640 --> 01:26:09,880
This is what they're like off-camera.

2309
01:26:09,880 --> 01:26:11,240
What is it with guys?

2310
01:26:11,240 --> 01:26:12,160
Xu, are you like this

2311
01:26:12,160 --> 01:26:13,040
with your friends too?

2312
01:26:13,040 --> 01:26:13,920
Just two guys

2313
01:26:13,920 --> 01:26:15,360
goofing around together?

2314
01:26:15,360 --> 01:26:16,160
Guys can get like this

2315
01:26:16,160 --> 01:26:16,920
when they're together.

2316
01:26:16,920 --> 01:26:18,080
Yeah, definitely.

2317
01:26:18,680 --> 01:26:20,440
Come on, let's go get a pump.

2318
01:26:20,440 --> 01:26:22,000
Let's hit the gym.

2319
01:26:22,000 --> 01:26:22,920
Yeah, let's go.

2320
01:26:24,200 --> 01:26:25,680
I still don't know
if I'll give it to her.

2321
01:26:25,680 --> 01:26:26,680
Maybe I'll give you one instead.

2322
01:26:27,080 --> 01:26:27,640
If you do...

2323
01:26:27,640 --> 01:26:28,400
If you give me yours,

2324
01:26:28,400 --> 01:26:29,480
we're getting a feast first.

2325
01:26:35,360 --> 01:26:36,480
Workout corner.

2326
01:26:39,000 --> 01:26:40,880
Sun Bohan's over there,
rolling out his butt.

2327
01:26:48,680 --> 01:26:49,480
Feel anything?

2328
01:26:49,480 --> 01:26:50,280
Yeah.

2329
01:26:50,840 --> 01:26:52,560
Why does this feel weirdly sad?

2330
01:26:52,560 --> 01:26:54,640
Why is nobody here?

2331
01:26:54,640 --> 01:26:56,240
When you're lonely, hit the gym.

2332
01:26:56,680 --> 01:26:57,080
Exactly.

2333
01:27:01,220 --> 01:27:02,060
(Looks back)

2334
01:27:02,560 --> 01:27:03,720
Think they're back?

2335
01:27:03,720 --> 01:27:04,480
I think so.

2336
01:27:06,240 --> 01:27:07,440
So what should I do?

2337
01:27:08,000 --> 01:27:09,640
Just keep doing what you're doing.

2338
01:27:09,640 --> 01:27:11,320
Be yourself.

2339
01:27:11,320 --> 01:27:13,020
(Oh)

2340
01:27:13,280 --> 01:27:14,520
Know when to hold on and let go.

2341
01:27:22,400 --> 01:27:23,760
They can't. They're done.

2342
01:27:25,800 --> 01:27:26,800
(Sha Yue'er and Chen Hewen return
from their date)

2343
01:27:26,800 --> 01:27:27,600
They're back.

2344
01:27:28,200 --> 01:27:29,520
We're back.

2345
01:27:30,640 --> 01:27:31,760
Someone went to the stargazing room.

2346
01:27:32,320 --> 01:27:33,080
Huh?

2347
01:27:33,360 --> 01:27:34,400
The light.

2348
01:27:34,400 --> 01:27:35,360
For the stargazing room?

2349
01:27:35,360 --> 01:27:35,840
Yeah.

2350
01:27:41,960 --> 01:27:42,720
If it lights up tonight,

2351
01:27:42,720 --> 01:27:43,760
does that mean tomorrow

2352
01:27:43,760 --> 01:27:45,600
they can...

2353
01:27:47,320 --> 01:27:48,120
Someone's there.

2354
01:27:48,120 --> 01:27:48,960
Downstair.

2355
01:27:50,280 --> 01:27:51,640
There are a lot of people.

2356
01:27:53,380 --> 01:27:54,900
(Looks around)

2357
01:27:54,920 --> 01:27:55,560
Here they come.

2358
01:27:56,360 --> 01:27:56,840
They're back.

2359
01:27:56,840 --> 01:27:57,960
They're both back.

2360
01:27:58,480 --> 01:27:59,720
Both of them.

2361
01:28:00,240 --> 01:28:01,680
Sha Yue'er has flowers.

2362
01:28:01,680 --> 01:28:03,000
Then...

2363
01:28:03,000 --> 01:28:03,480
I...

2364
01:28:03,480 --> 01:28:04,440
I should put on my shoes.

2365
01:28:06,800 --> 01:28:08,160
This is kind of awkward.

2366
01:28:08,800 --> 01:28:10,080
What's he even going to say?

2367
01:28:13,500 --> 01:28:14,220
(Looks)

2368
01:28:14,240 --> 01:28:15,520
Chen Hewen feels totally different.

2369
01:28:15,520 --> 01:28:16,360
(Looks again)
Look.

2370
01:28:17,000 --> 01:28:19,040
Do those shoes fit?

2371
01:28:19,040 --> 01:28:20,000
Yeah.

2372
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:20,900
(Crouches)

2373
01:28:20,980 --> 01:28:22,520
(Crouches)

2374
01:28:22,520 --> 01:28:23,040
Pretty much.

2375
01:28:23,040 --> 01:28:24,160
I can't even get mine on.

2376
01:28:26,040 --> 01:28:27,480
I need to run inside
to use the bathroom.

2377
01:28:27,480 --> 01:28:28,040
Is that okay

2378
01:28:28,040 --> 01:28:28,960
with you,

2379
01:28:28,960 --> 01:28:29,760
Sha Yue'er?

2380
01:28:29,760 --> 01:28:30,440
Sure.

2381
01:28:30,820 --> 01:28:32,000
(Walks past)

2382
01:28:32,000 --> 01:28:32,920
He missed his chance.

2383
01:28:33,140 --> 01:28:34,980
(Back turned)

2384
01:28:38,800 --> 01:28:39,760
By the time he got his shoes on,

2385
01:28:39,760 --> 01:28:40,840
she was already upstairs.

2386
01:28:42,840 --> 01:28:43,480
See?

2387
01:28:47,120 --> 01:28:48,120
He saw it.

2388
01:28:49,460 --> 01:28:50,740
(Looks back)

2389
01:28:50,940 --> 01:28:52,060
(Looks again)

2390
01:29:01,360 --> 01:29:02,000
Forget it.

2391
01:29:02,000 --> 01:29:03,900
(Forget it)

2392
01:29:05,120 --> 01:29:06,640
Even courage has its limits.

2393
01:29:06,640 --> 01:29:07,640
So do feelings.

2394
01:29:11,060 --> 01:29:12,260
(Holds the door)

2395
01:29:13,600 --> 01:29:15,640
You finally held the door for me.

2396
01:29:17,400 --> 01:29:18,320
What?

2397
01:29:18,320 --> 01:29:19,840
Exactly!

2398
01:29:19,840 --> 01:29:20,880
(Looks back)
Where are my shoes?

2399
01:29:21,800 --> 01:29:22,640
Which ones are yours?

2400
01:29:22,640 --> 01:29:23,760
The blue ones.

2401
01:29:23,880 --> 01:29:25,440
Thanks.

2402
01:29:25,480 --> 01:29:27,960
Who's back?

2403
01:29:28,400 --> 01:29:29,080
Liang Xiaoyu.

2404
01:29:31,600 --> 01:29:33,240
So pretty.

2405
01:29:34,800 --> 01:29:36,560
Hey, everyone.

2406
01:29:37,080 --> 01:29:39,320
Hey, guys.

2407
01:29:40,560 --> 01:29:41,200
Hi.

2408
01:29:42,880 --> 01:29:44,440
My sweet Cui Kaiyi.

2409
01:29:44,440 --> 01:29:45,760
Sha Yue'er, you're back!

2410
01:29:45,760 --> 01:29:46,400
I'm back.

2411
01:29:47,420 --> 01:29:48,260
(Jogging over)

2412
01:29:48,680 --> 01:29:49,880
How was it?

2413
01:29:50,320 --> 01:29:51,080
Good.

2414
01:29:51,080 --> 01:29:51,920
Pretty good.

2415
01:29:51,920 --> 01:29:52,320
Fun.

2416
01:29:52,320 --> 01:29:53,440
Not bad.

2417
01:29:54,040 --> 01:29:54,680
Flowers!

2418
01:29:56,520 --> 01:29:58,440
They look like the ones from last time.

2419
01:29:59,200 --> 01:30:00,120
The same person gave them to me.

2420
01:30:00,120 --> 01:30:02,000
(Flowers from the same person)
I knew they looked familiar.

2421
01:30:02,000 --> 01:30:02,960
The same person.

2422
01:30:04,200 --> 01:30:05,360
The same exact style.

2423
01:30:05,360 --> 01:30:06,520
So pretty.

2424
01:30:07,000 --> 01:30:08,480
Who went to the stargazing room?

2425
01:30:09,000 --> 01:30:10,680
Cui Yihang and Si.

2426
01:30:11,600 --> 01:30:12,640
They're inside.

2427
01:30:13,560 --> 01:30:14,680
They already went in.

2428
01:30:15,720 --> 01:30:17,440
Quick, adjust my hand.

2429
01:30:18,400 --> 01:30:19,600
You guys look so pretty.

2430
01:30:20,560 --> 01:30:21,520
You go upstairs first.

2431
01:30:21,520 --> 01:30:22,280
Later, we'll...

2432
01:30:22,280 --> 01:30:24,000
Bye!

2433
01:30:24,600 --> 01:30:25,400
I need to use the bathroom first.

2434
01:30:25,400 --> 01:30:26,040
I'll go ahead.

2435
01:30:26,040 --> 01:30:26,640
Okay.

2436
01:30:50,720 --> 01:30:51,480
She's happy.

2437
01:30:51,480 --> 01:30:52,460
(Happy)

2438
01:30:53,680 --> 01:30:56,240
Some are happy. Some are not so much.

2439
01:30:57,920 --> 01:30:58,720
I can't stop.

2440
01:30:58,720 --> 01:30:59,880
I seriously can't.

2441
01:31:00,440 --> 01:31:01,560
I can't.

2442
01:31:02,480 --> 01:31:04,200
I'm going downstairs to get some food.

2443
01:31:09,160 --> 01:31:10,520
I kind of don't want to go back.

2444
01:31:10,520 --> 01:31:11,580
(Doesn't want to go back)

2445
01:31:11,580 --> 01:31:12,600
You have to eventually.

2446
01:31:12,600 --> 01:31:14,040
You can't avoid it forever.

2447
01:31:14,600 --> 01:31:16,040
I don't even want to open my eyes.

2448
01:31:16,040 --> 01:31:17,800
I wish I'd imagined all of this.

2449
01:31:19,600 --> 01:31:21,440
None of this

2450
01:31:21,440 --> 01:31:23,680
makes any sense

2451
01:31:23,680 --> 01:31:25,000
to me right now.

2452
01:31:26,600 --> 01:31:28,080
Did you see them?

2453
01:31:28,760 --> 01:31:29,760
Yeah.

2454
01:31:30,240 --> 01:31:31,760
But they didn't come over.

2455
01:31:31,760 --> 01:31:32,880
They didn't even say hi.

2456
01:31:32,880 --> 01:31:33,680
That hurts.

2457
01:31:35,040 --> 01:31:36,000
Maybe

2458
01:31:36,000 --> 01:31:36,760
they actually

2459
01:31:36,760 --> 01:31:37,400
saw you too.

2460
01:31:37,400 --> 01:31:38,480
They just felt...

2461
01:31:38,480 --> 01:31:39,760
A little awkward.

2462
01:31:49,820 --> 01:31:50,900
(Looks)

2463
01:31:57,520 --> 01:31:58,440
They ran into each other.

2464
01:32:00,480 --> 01:32:01,520
Sit for a bit.

2465
01:32:01,520 --> 01:32:02,800
I'll get some water.

2466
01:32:03,640 --> 01:32:04,440
Almost done.

2467
01:32:04,440 --> 01:32:04,800
Okay.

2468
01:32:05,160 --> 01:32:06,040
How was your day?

2469
01:32:07,160 --> 01:32:08,000
It was good.

2470
01:32:08,320 --> 01:32:09,040
When we got back,

2471
01:32:09,040 --> 01:32:10,200
the stargazing room was lit up.

2472
01:32:11,880 --> 01:32:12,840
Uh...

2473
01:32:13,840 --> 01:32:14,680
I can't tell you.

2474
01:32:14,680 --> 01:32:16,760
Just look who's missing.

2475
01:32:16,960 --> 01:32:18,000
I saw Cui Yihang.

2476
01:32:18,000 --> 01:32:18,720
Yeah.

2477
01:32:18,720 --> 01:32:19,800
Better not say too much.

2478
01:32:24,280 --> 01:32:25,240
Where'd you guys go?

2479
01:32:25,240 --> 01:32:26,120
You were out so late.

2480
01:32:26,560 --> 01:32:27,600
(Asks anyway)
He asked anyway.

2481
01:32:30,520 --> 01:32:31,040
Remember

2482
01:32:31,040 --> 01:32:32,360
that misunderstanding we had?

2483
01:32:32,840 --> 01:32:34,560
We talked it out.

2484
01:32:35,200 --> 01:32:37,000
Otherwise, we'd both

2485
01:32:37,000 --> 01:32:37,760
still feel bad.

2486
01:32:39,520 --> 01:32:40,920
Now Zhao Xilun's the one who feels bad.

2487
01:32:42,800 --> 01:32:43,480
Sit for a bit.

2488
01:32:43,840 --> 01:32:44,400
Sit down.

2489
01:33:03,240 --> 01:33:04,240
Hello.

2490
01:33:05,280 --> 01:33:06,120
Hello.

2491
01:33:07,400 --> 01:33:08,800
Hello.

2492
01:33:08,800 --> 01:33:10,140
(Looks up)
Hello.

2493
01:33:11,340 --> 01:33:13,340
(Closes eyes)

2494
01:33:13,360 --> 01:33:15,680
There are so many people.

2495
01:33:15,680 --> 01:33:16,720
Fang,

2496
01:33:17,000 --> 01:33:18,200
I grabbed one of these.

2497
01:33:18,600 --> 01:33:19,280
Go get one.

2498
01:33:19,280 --> 01:33:20,080
There's more.

2499
01:33:20,080 --> 01:33:21,720
Don't forget yours.

2500
01:33:21,720 --> 01:33:23,080
Breakfast is downstairs.

2501
01:33:23,520 --> 01:33:24,560
They got bird's nest drinks.

2502
01:33:25,440 --> 01:33:26,400
I'll go grab one.

2503
01:33:29,720 --> 01:33:31,360
We get a little treat too.

2504
01:33:35,100 --> 01:33:37,180
(Changing Liang Renfang's dressing)

2505
01:33:41,730 --> 01:33:42,490
Oh my God.

2506
01:33:42,640 --> 01:33:43,360
Thanks, Chen Hewen.

2507
01:33:43,360 --> 01:33:44,120
Thanks.

2508
01:33:44,120 --> 01:33:45,880
He's so good at taking care of everyone.

2509
01:33:52,720 --> 01:33:54,360
Where'd you guys go?

2510
01:33:54,360 --> 01:33:55,840
Badminton.

2511
01:33:56,640 --> 01:33:58,000
You played badminton on your date?

2512
01:33:58,000 --> 01:33:59,160
Seriously?

2513
01:34:00,680 --> 01:34:01,720
I'll just smile.

2514
01:34:01,720 --> 01:34:02,720
Chen Hewen.

2515
01:34:04,800 --> 01:34:06,160
That was your home turf.

2516
01:34:06,480 --> 01:34:07,520
(Home turf)
Not really.

2517
01:34:07,520 --> 01:34:08,560
I was just messing around.

2518
01:34:12,660 --> 01:34:14,820
(Looks back and forth)

2519
01:34:16,600 --> 01:34:17,400
That hurts.

2520
01:34:22,680 --> 01:34:23,520
Then what?

2521
01:34:24,320 --> 01:34:24,880
That's it.

2522
01:34:24,880 --> 01:34:25,320
Dinner?

2523
01:34:25,320 --> 01:34:26,280
Yeah.

2524
01:34:27,860 --> 01:34:28,700
(Looks over)

2525
01:34:29,520 --> 01:34:30,800
She's really good.

2526
01:34:30,800 --> 01:34:31,740
(Praising her)

2527
01:34:32,640 --> 01:34:33,880
He's complimenting her
in front of everyone.

2528
01:34:33,880 --> 01:34:34,840
Thanks.

2529
01:34:36,800 --> 01:34:38,400
He's all over the place right now.

2530
01:34:40,880 --> 01:34:41,880
It's complicated.

2531
01:34:43,720 --> 01:34:46,120
Look. Everyone's in their own corner.

2532
01:34:46,120 --> 01:34:47,280
One person per corner.

2533
01:34:53,640 --> 01:34:55,040
This tension is unreal.

2534
01:35:02,840 --> 01:35:04,320
This is so boring.

2535
01:35:50,680 --> 01:35:52,000
You look good. Where are you going?

2536
01:35:52,600 --> 01:35:54,450
Yeah, I know I look good.

2537
01:35:54,450 --> 01:35:55,270
You do.

2538
01:35:57,160 --> 01:35:58,240
I'm going to play piano.

2539
01:35:58,240 --> 01:35:58,840
Go ahead.

2540
01:36:00,720 --> 01:36:02,160
I'll take some photos for you too.

2541
01:36:02,160 --> 01:36:03,000
Okay.

2542
01:36:03,000 --> 01:36:03,680
Let's go.

2543
01:36:03,680 --> 01:36:03,960
Sure.

2544
01:36:03,960 --> 01:36:05,600
Let's go downstairs for some photos.

2545
01:36:05,960 --> 01:36:06,680
Let's go.

2546
01:36:08,000 --> 01:36:08,920
This camera isn't doing me any favors.

2547
01:36:08,920 --> 01:36:09,720
Sit over here.

2548
01:36:09,720 --> 01:36:11,160
Don't sit on the floor.

2549
01:36:14,480 --> 01:36:15,440
What an awkward vibe.

2550
01:36:16,320 --> 01:36:17,800
Let's go.

2551
01:36:19,240 --> 01:36:21,680
I'm scared to use it.

2552
01:36:21,680 --> 01:36:23,080
What'd you guys do today?

2553
01:36:23,080 --> 01:36:24,480
Just walked around.

2554
01:36:24,480 --> 01:36:25,520
Just walked around?

2555
01:36:25,800 --> 01:36:26,760
In Beijing?

2556
01:36:27,440 --> 01:36:28,400
We went back and forth.

2557
01:36:28,400 --> 01:36:29,800
Back and forth?

2558
01:36:31,840 --> 01:36:32,920
Hebei and Beijing.

2559
01:36:53,720 --> 01:36:54,840
She needs a distraction.

2560
01:37:09,360 --> 01:37:10,480
Tomorrow I'll take

2561
01:37:10,480 --> 01:37:11,640
some really good photos of you two.

2562
01:37:12,560 --> 01:37:14,120
